{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 123, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1->3 absent, a direct conv path 0->3 restores much more of the output node's input (exp 3 vs 1-2)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0->3 when edge 1->3 is also absent starves the output node and can disconnect the cell (exp 72, 74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 1->3 when edge 2->3 is absent leaves the output with too few or no incoming paths (exp 43, 44)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv into the output matters much more when edge 0->3 is missing (exp 17)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In parameter-free skip-dominated cells, another skip on 0->3 short-circuits learning, while conv-heavy cells benefit from the residual (exp 38 vs 31-34)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a first trainable conv to a skip-dominated cell gives very large gains compared with conv-rich parents (exp 28-29 vs 21-27)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv on edge 2->3 rescues collapsed parameter-free cells but adds little to conv-rich ones (exp 85 vs 11-20)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing the conv on 0->2 is nearly harmless when other convs remain, but devastating when it is the only conv (exp 51-60 vs 54, 59)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "An extra conv on 1->2 is redundant when edge 0->1 is already a 3x3 conv, but helpful in skip or 1x1 cells (exp 61-67 vs 68-69)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where no 0->3 path existed helps more than swapping out an existing conv or pool on that edge (exp 31-34, 39-40 vs 36-37)."}], "tok": 17384, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_con